# M3.2 acceptance, session 1 of 3: selection and copy on tests/data/sample.pdf
# (3 US Letter pages; page 1 has the heading "Page One", a 3-line paragraph
# "The quick brown fox ... exists to / test PDF loading, ... Marker / word:
# zebra." and the page number "1"; page 2 starts "Page Two" / "Attention is all
# you need."). Run all three sessions with tests/acceptance/m3.2.sh, which
# builds the clipboard reader and writes the expected texts that each
# `run .../clipcheck <name>` compares the clipboard with (exact bytes). This
# session is
#   scripts/shot.sh -o <out>/sample -s tests/acceptance/m3.2.steps -- \
#     env HOME=/tmp/agentic-reader-m3.2/home ./build/app/agentic-reader tests/data/sample.pdf
#
# Interface choices where the spec is silent (see also tests/test_selection.cpp):
#   - A drag selects every box from the box under the press to the box under the
#     release, in reading order, either direction. Double-click selects the word
#     under the pointer, triple-click its line. A click (no drag) on empty page
#     space or the grey margin clears the selection.
#   - Copied text joins words with a space where the PDF has one, lines with
#     "\n", pages with "\n", and nothing after the last word.
#   - Right-click opens the context menu without changing the selection. Its
#     first item is "&Copy" (wxID_COPY, may show "Ctrl+C"), enabled only with a
#     selection. The steps pick it by its mnemonic: `key c` while the menu is open.
#   - Ctrl+C (or Copy) with no selection leaves the clipboard unchanged.
#   - The highlight is the theme's selection colour at 35% alpha over the words'
#     boxes, so the words stay readable through it. Under Xvfb's default GTK theme
#     that is a light blue.
#   - The I-beam cursor over text is not visible in screenshots (import does not
#     capture the pointer). human check: hover over text and over the margin.
#
# Geometry at the default window (1400x900 at the screen origin), measured on
# the M3.1 build: menu bar y 0..24, toolbar y 25..66 (zoom combo at (35,45)),
# PDF pane x 225..980 and y 67..877. At fit width ("119%", zoom 731/612) page 1
# is at x 237..967 and its top edge at y 79, so a point (x, y) in page points is
# at (237 + 1.1944 x, 79 + 1.1944 y). Word centres used below: "The" (381,271),
# "quick" (413,271), "brown" (451,271), "rendering," (513,289), "zebra."
# (428,306). If the toolbar height differs, every y shifts by the same amount.
wait 3

# Focus the PDF view with a click on empty page space below the paragraph.
click 600 600
wait 1

# Start: page 1 of sample.pdf at fit width, combo "119%", entry "1 / 3".
# Nothing is highlighted.
shot start

drag 375 271 430 306
wait 1

# Drag from "The" to "zebra.": the whole paragraph is highlighted, all of line
# 1 ("The" .. "to"), all of line 2 ("test" .. "Marker") and line 3 "word:
# zebra.", with a translucent light-blue fill over each word box (gaps between
# words may or may not be filled). The black text is clearly readable through
# the fill. "Page One" and the page number are not highlighted.
shot drag-paragraph

key ctrl+c
wait 1
run /tmp/agentic-reader-m3.2/clipcheck paragraph

dblclick 451 271
wait 1

# Double-click on "brown": only the word "brown" is highlighted. The paragraph
# highlight is gone.
shot dblclick-word

key ctrl+c
wait 1
run /tmp/agentic-reader-m3.2/clipcheck word

tripleclick 513 289
wait 1

# Triple-click on "rendering,": the whole second line of the paragraph, "test
# PDF loading, rendering, and text extraction in Agentic Reader. Marker", is
# highlighted, and nothing on lines 1 and 3. "brown" is no longer highlighted.
shot tripleclick-line

key ctrl+c
wait 1
run /tmp/agentic-reader-m3.2/clipcheck line

drag 430 306 413 271
wait 1

# Backward drag from "zebra." up to "quick": the paragraph from "quick" to
# "zebra." is highlighted; "The" at the start of line 1 is not.
shot drag-backward

click 451 271 3
wait 1

# Right-click on "brown" inside the selection: a popup menu at the pointer whose
# first item is "Copy" (enabled, black text; it may show "Ctrl+C"). The
# highlight from "quick" to "zebra." is unchanged where the menu does not cover it.
shot context-menu

key c
wait 1
run /tmp/agentic-reader-m3.2/clipcheck backward-menu

click 600 600
wait 1

# Click on empty page space: the menu is gone and nothing is highlighted.
shot cleared

# Ctrl+C with no selection keeps the last copied text.
key ctrl+c
wait 1
run /tmp/agentic-reader-m3.2/clipcheck backward-menu

click 600 600 3
wait 1

# Right-click with no selection: the popup menu shows "Copy" greyed out
# (disabled). Nothing is highlighted.
shot context-menu-disabled

key Escape
wait 1

# Cross-page selection at 60%: two pages in view. Page rects at 60% are
# 367x475px, x 419..785; page 1 from y 79, page 2 from y 566 after Home.
# "zebra." is at (515,193) on page 1, "Attention" at (500,663) on page 2.
click 35 45
key ctrl+a
type 60
key Return
wait 2
click 300 400
key Home
wait 2

# Combo "60%". Page 1 (x 419..785, y 79..553) with "Page One" and the
# paragraph, then the grey gap, then page 2 from y 566 with "Page Two" and
# "Attention is all you need." Nothing is highlighted.
shot zoom-60

drag 515 193 500 663
wait 1

# Drag from "zebra." on page 1 to "Attention" on page 2: highlighted are
# "zebra." and the page number "1" on page 1, and "Page Two" and "Attention" on
# page 2. Nothing else ("word:", "is all you need.") is highlighted. Each
# highlight sits exactly on its word at this zoom.
shot cross-page

key ctrl+c
wait 1
run /tmp/agentic-reader-m3.2/clipcheck cross-page

# Zoom back to fit width with the selection kept.
key ctrl+0
key Home
wait 2

# Fit width ("119%"), page 1 at the top. The highlight followed the zoom: it
# covers exactly "zebra." on line 3 (at about x 409..446, y 299..312). The page
# number "1" (about y 908) is below the pane. No highlight anywhere else.
shot selection-after-zoom
